# keep-it-in-your-box — user preferences.
#
# Copy to  ~/.keep-it-in-your-box/config  (chmod 600). HOST-ONLY: this file is never
# bind-mounted into the sandbox, so the agent cannot read or rewrite what governs its own
# credentials and egress. Format is `key = value`; unknown keys are ignored; comments start
# with '#'. All keys are optional and the defaults preserve today's behaviour.

# ── Credential broker ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hold the real Claude token host-side and hand the sandbox only a placeholder + an
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL pointed at a broker sidecar (no token in the container; audit H3/H4).
# ON by default. KIB_BROKER=1 / KIB_BROKER=0 override this per launch.
#
# The brokered credential is a LONG-LIVED STATIC token, stored next to this file as
# `claude-token` (mode 600) — NOT ~/.claude/.credentials.json, whose refresh tokens
# are single-use and rotate, so a second refresher logs you out. The first interactive
# launch with no token offers the login for you; decline it (or launch headless) and the
# session falls back to mounting the real credential, with a warning.
#
#   kib broker login      # wraps `claude setup-token`, stores + probes the result
#   kib broker status     # is the stored token still accepted? (never prints it)
#   kib broker logout     # remove it
broker = on

